WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.170
In one set of illustrative data, a cereal
crop sown thinly makes about 120 seeds

2
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:07.360
per plant.

3
00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:12.860
Sow the same crop very densely,
and each plant makes only about 25.

4
00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:17.900
Same water, same feed for every
plot, and only one species growing.

5
00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.600
Yet each plant does far worse.

6
00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:24.870
So why do members of one species often
compete harder with each other than with

7
00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:26.730
any other species?

8
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:30.650
In this mission, you'll pin
down what competition really is,

9
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:33.070
and why it needs no fight at all.

10
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.110
Then you'll watch growth curves
change when a second species moves in,

11
00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.470
and again when it is removed.

12
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:44.480
Your mission: explain why members of one
species often compete hardest with each

13
00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:45.010
other.
